{title: Make A Joyful Noise}
{artist: Larry Holder}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 80}

Verse 1
and let me know what you think of this song and/or this method
of outreach.

Verse 2
Mark is a computer programmer and composer in London, England.
He wrote the music and sequenced the MIDI, and I added the words.
Mark plans to build a website for his songs, and til then I'll
host our collaborations here, of which this song is a first.

Verse 3
MAKE A JOYFUL NOISE
Music by Mark Wilkinson, Words by Larry Holder
Copyright (C) 1998 Mark Wilkinson and Larry Holder

Verse 4
(8-measure intro)

Verse 5
Lift your voice and let us sing His praise,
And make a joyful noise.
Glorify the Lord in all our ways,
With songs of our thanksgiving!

Verse 6
Glory be to the Father,
And to His Son;
Glory unto the Spirit
In whom believers now are one!

Verse 7
Sing to Him our praises;
Give Him praise in all that we do.
He's our Rock and Salvation:
In Him we know that we are born anew!

Verse 8
(7-measure instrumental, then repeat lyrics)
